<title>USA: Minnesota corn harvest finished in most areas.</title>
<headline>Minnesota corn harvest finished in most areas.</headline>
<dateline>ST PAUL, Minn. 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minnesota's corn harvest was mostly complete as of Sunday, as freezing conditions allowed farmers good access to remaining stands of corn, said the state's agricultural statistics service in its latest crop report.</p>
<p>Corn was 95 percent harvested, up from 88 percent a week earlier and ahead of the five-year average of 88 percent.</p>
<p>Progress ranged from 99 percent complete in the northwest district to 86 percent in the southeast.</p>
<p>Moisture conditions of corn harvested averaged 19 percent, versus 17 percent last year and an average of 21 percent.</p>
<p>Topsoil moisture was rated 22 percent surplus, 74 percent adequate and four percent short.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk 312-408 8720</p>
</text>
